# Tests — Annex C defined terms (C-2)

Assertion-based tests for the six definitions of C-2. Each definition is a
boundary: a Payroll Week starts on one particular day, a Night Hour starts
within one particular window, a Grade is read as at one particular date, and a
Critical Incident Response falls inside one particular period. Every one of
those boundaries is tested from both sides, because a definition that is off
by one day or one hour silently mis-prices every entitlement computed from it.

Counterexamples found by the adversarial reviewer are kept separately, in
`tests/counterexamples/`, and are re-run by `scripts/check.sh`.

> Using WorkingTimeDefs as WTD

## C2_1_BaseHourlyRate

C-2.1: an annual salary that is an exact multiple of 2,080 cents divides
without remainder.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_1_BaseHourlyRate:
  output r content WTD.BaseHourlyRate

scope TestC2_1_BaseHourlyRate:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.BaseHourlyRate with {
      -- annual_base_salary: $52,000.00
    }
  assertion r.base_hourly_rate = 25.0
  assertion r.base_hourly_rate_to_the_penny = $25.00
```

## C2_1_BaseHourlyRateIsExact

C-2.1: 50,000 / 2,080 = 24.0384615... , which does not terminate. The clause
states a division and no rounding, so the rate is held as an exact decimal and
the assertion is stated as the exact rational rather than as a rounded literal
-- asserting 24.04 would pin the very rounding the clause does not authorise.
The penny figure is asserted separately, and exists for display only.

An earlier version held the rate as `money`, which rounded it before any
premium was applied and mis-paid a 50-hour week in both directions depending
on the salary. See tests/counterexamples/CE-0023.yaml.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_1_BaseHourlyRateIsExact:
  output r content WTD.BaseHourlyRate

scope TestC2_1_BaseHourlyRateIsExact:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.BaseHourlyRate with {
      -- annual_base_salary: $50,000.00
    }
  assertion r.base_hourly_rate * 2080.0 = 50000.0
  assertion r.base_hourly_rate_to_the_penny = $24.04
```

## C2_1_BaseHourlyRateZero

C-2.1: a zero salary yields a zero rate rather than an error.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_1_BaseHourlyRateZero:
  output r content WTD.BaseHourlyRate

scope TestC2_1_BaseHourlyRateZero:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.BaseHourlyRate with {
      -- annual_base_salary: $0.00
    }
  assertion r.base_hourly_rate = 0.0
  assertion r.base_hourly_rate_to_the_penny = $0.00
```

## C2_2_WeekFromItsMonday

C-2.2: a Monday is the first day of its own Payroll Week.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_2_WeekFromItsMonday:
  output r content WTD.PayrollWeekOf

scope TestC2_2_WeekFromItsMonday:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.PayrollWeekOf with { -- calendar_day: |2024-01-08| }
  assertion r.days_since_monday = 0
  assertion r.payroll_week.first_day = |2024-01-08|
  assertion r.payroll_week.last_day = |2024-01-14|
```

## C2_2_WeekFromItsSunday

C-2.2: the Sunday is the last day of the week that began six days earlier, not
the first day of a new one. This is the other side of the week boundary.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_2_WeekFromItsSunday:
  output r content WTD.PayrollWeekOf

scope TestC2_2_WeekFromItsSunday:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.PayrollWeekOf with { -- calendar_day: |2024-01-07| }
  assertion r.days_since_monday = 6
  assertion r.payroll_week.first_day = |2024-01-01|
  assertion r.payroll_week.last_day = |2024-01-07|
```

## C2_2_WeekFromMidWeek

C-2.2: a Wednesday resolves to the same week as its Monday.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_2_WeekFromMidWeek:
  output r content WTD.PayrollWeekOf

scope TestC2_2_WeekFromMidWeek:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.PayrollWeekOf with { -- calendar_day: |2024-01-10| }
  assertion r.days_since_monday = 2
  assertion r.payroll_week.first_day = |2024-01-08|
  assertion r.payroll_week.last_day = |2024-01-14|
```

## C2_2_WeekSpansMonthAndLeapDay

C-2.2: seven consecutive days, so a Payroll Week may straddle a month end. The
week containing Friday 1 March 2024 begins on 26 February and contains the
leap day.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_2_WeekSpansMonthAndLeapDay:
  output r content WTD.PayrollWeekOf

scope TestC2_2_WeekSpansMonthAndLeapDay:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.PayrollWeekOf with { -- calendar_day: |2024-03-01| }
  assertion r.days_since_monday = 4
  assertion r.payroll_week.first_day = |2024-02-26|
  assertion r.payroll_week.last_day = |2024-03-03|
```

## C2_3_NightHour21

C-2.3: the hour beginning at 21:00 ends at 22:00 and is not a Night Hour. This
is the lower boundary from below.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_3_NightHour21:
  output r content WTD.NightHours

scope TestC2_3_NightHour21:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.NightHours with { -- hour_beginning: 21 }
  assertion r.is_night_hour = false
```

## C2_3_NightHour22

C-2.3: the hour beginning at 22:00 is the first Night Hour.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_3_NightHour22:
  output r content WTD.NightHours

scope TestC2_3_NightHour22:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.NightHours with { -- hour_beginning: 22 }
  assertion r.is_night_hour = true
```

## C2_3_NightHourMidnight

C-2.3: 'and 06:00 on the following day' carries the window across midnight.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_3_NightHourMidnight:
  output r content WTD.NightHours

scope TestC2_3_NightHourMidnight:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.NightHours with { -- hour_beginning: 0 }
  assertion r.is_night_hour = true
```

## C2_3_NightHour5

C-2.3: the hour beginning at 05:00 ends at 06:00 and is the last Night Hour.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_3_NightHour5:
  output r content WTD.NightHours

scope TestC2_3_NightHour5:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.NightHours with { -- hour_beginning: 5 }
  assertion r.is_night_hour = true
```

## C2_3_NightHour6

C-2.3: the hour beginning at 06:00 is outside the window. This is the upper
boundary from above.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_3_NightHour6:
  output r content WTD.NightHours

scope TestC2_3_NightHour6:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.NightHours with { -- hour_beginning: 6 }
  assertion r.is_night_hour = false
```

## C2_3_NightHourNoon

C-2.3: the middle of the day is not a Night Hour.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_3_NightHourNoon:
  output r content WTD.NightHours

scope TestC2_3_NightHourNoon:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.NightHours with { -- hour_beginning: 12 }
  assertion r.is_night_hour = false
```

## C2_4_GradeLatestRecordingInForce

C-2.4: where two recordings are in force at the first day of the week, the
later one governs.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_4_GradeLatestRecordingInForce:
  output r content WTD.GradeForPayrollWeek

scope TestC2_4_GradeLatestRecordingInForce:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.GradeForPayrollWeek with {
      -- grade_records: [
           WTD.GradeRecord { -- grade: 3 -- recorded_from: |2023-01-01| };
           WTD.GradeRecord { -- grade: 5 -- recorded_from: |2024-01-01| }
         ]
      -- payroll_week: WTD.PayrollWeek {
           -- first_day: |2024-01-08|
           -- last_day: |2024-01-14|
         }
    }
  assertion r.grade = Present content 5
```

## C2_4_GradeRecordedOnFirstDayOfWeek

C-2.4: 'at the first day of the Payroll Week' includes that day, so a
recording made on the Monday governs that Monday's week.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_4_GradeRecordedOnFirstDayOfWeek:
  output r content WTD.GradeForPayrollWeek

scope TestC2_4_GradeRecordedOnFirstDayOfWeek:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.GradeForPayrollWeek with {
      -- grade_records: [
           WTD.GradeRecord { -- grade: 3 -- recorded_from: |2023-01-01| };
           WTD.GradeRecord { -- grade: 5 -- recorded_from: |2024-01-08| }
         ]
      -- payroll_week: WTD.PayrollWeek {
           -- first_day: |2024-01-08|
           -- last_day: |2024-01-14|
         }
    }
  assertion r.grade = Present content 5
```

## C2_4_GradeRecordedAfterFirstDayOfWeek

C-2.4: the other side of the as-of boundary. A promotion recorded on the
Tuesday does not govern the week that began on the Monday, even though it
takes effect during that week.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_4_GradeRecordedAfterFirstDayOfWeek:
  output r content WTD.GradeForPayrollWeek

scope TestC2_4_GradeRecordedAfterFirstDayOfWeek:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.GradeForPayrollWeek with {
      -- grade_records: [
           WTD.GradeRecord { -- grade: 3 -- recorded_from: |2023-01-01| };
           WTD.GradeRecord { -- grade: 5 -- recorded_from: |2024-01-09| }
         ]
      -- payroll_week: WTD.PayrollWeek {
           -- first_day: |2024-01-08|
           -- last_day: |2024-01-14|
         }
    }
  assertion r.grade = Present content 3
```

## C2_4_GradeNoRecordingInForce

C-2.4: where the system of record holds nothing in force at the first day of
the week, the Annex supplies no Grade. The result is `Absent`; it is not zero.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_4_GradeNoRecordingInForce:
  output r content WTD.GradeForPayrollWeek

scope TestC2_4_GradeNoRecordingInForce:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.GradeForPayrollWeek with {
      -- grade_records: [
           WTD.GradeRecord { -- grade: 5 -- recorded_from: |2024-02-01| }
         ]
      -- payroll_week: WTD.PayrollWeek {
           -- first_day: |2024-01-08|
           -- last_day: |2024-01-14|
         }
    }
  assertion r.grade = Absent
```

## C2_4_GradeEmptySystemOfRecord

C-2.4: an empty record is the same case.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_4_GradeEmptySystemOfRecord:
  output r content WTD.GradeForPayrollWeek

scope TestC2_4_GradeEmptySystemOfRecord:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.GradeForPayrollWeek with {
      -- grade_records: []
      -- payroll_week: WTD.PayrollWeek {
           -- first_day: |2024-01-08|
           -- last_day: |2024-01-14|
         }
    }
  assertion r.grade = Absent
```

## C2_5_Severity1WithinPeriod

C-2.5: all three limbs satisfied.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_5_Severity1WithinPeriod:
  output r content WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse

scope TestC2_5_Severity1WithinPeriod:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse with {
      -- incident: WTD.CriticalIncident {
           -- severity: 1
           -- declared_at: |2024-05-06|
           -- closed_at: Present content |2024-05-09|
         }
      -- work_performed_at: |2024-05-07|
      -- performed_in_response_to_incident: true
    }
  assertion r.within_incident_period = true
  assertion r.is_critical_incident_response = true
```

## C2_5_Severity2NotCritical

C-2.5: the severity threshold. Severity 2 is not Severity 1, even though the
work falls squarely inside the incident period.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_5_Severity2NotCritical:
  output r content WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse

scope TestC2_5_Severity2NotCritical:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse with {
      -- incident: WTD.CriticalIncident {
           -- severity: 2
           -- declared_at: |2024-05-06|
           -- closed_at: Present content |2024-05-09|
         }
      -- work_performed_at: |2024-05-07|
      -- performed_in_response_to_incident: true
    }
  assertion r.within_incident_period = true
  assertion r.is_critical_incident_response = false
```

## C2_5_DayBeforeDeclaration

C-2.5: the period runs 'from declaration', so the day before is outside it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_5_DayBeforeDeclaration:
  output r content WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse

scope TestC2_5_DayBeforeDeclaration:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse with {
      -- incident: WTD.CriticalIncident {
           -- severity: 1
           -- declared_at: |2024-05-06|
           -- closed_at: Present content |2024-05-09|
         }
      -- work_performed_at: |2024-05-05|
      -- performed_in_response_to_incident: true
    }
  assertion r.within_incident_period = false
  assertion r.is_critical_incident_response = false
```

## C2_5_DayOfDeclaration

C-2.5: the declaration day itself is inside the period.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_5_DayOfDeclaration:
  output r content WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse

scope TestC2_5_DayOfDeclaration:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse with {
      -- incident: WTD.CriticalIncident {
           -- severity: 1
           -- declared_at: |2024-05-06|
           -- closed_at: Present content |2024-05-09|
         }
      -- work_performed_at: |2024-05-06|
      -- performed_in_response_to_incident: true
    }
  assertion r.within_incident_period = true
  assertion r.is_critical_incident_response = true
```

## C2_5_DayOfClosure

C-2.5: the period runs 'until its formal closure', and the closure day is
treated as inside it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_5_DayOfClosure:
  output r content WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse

scope TestC2_5_DayOfClosure:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse with {
      -- incident: WTD.CriticalIncident {
           -- severity: 1
           -- declared_at: |2024-05-06|
           -- closed_at: Present content |2024-05-09|
         }
      -- work_performed_at: |2024-05-09|
      -- performed_in_response_to_incident: true
    }
  assertion r.within_incident_period = true
  assertion r.is_critical_incident_response = true
```

## C2_5_DayAfterClosure

C-2.5: the other side of the closure boundary.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_5_DayAfterClosure:
  output r content WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse

scope TestC2_5_DayAfterClosure:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse with {
      -- incident: WTD.CriticalIncident {
           -- severity: 1
           -- declared_at: |2024-05-06|
           -- closed_at: Present content |2024-05-09|
         }
      -- work_performed_at: |2024-05-10|
      -- performed_in_response_to_incident: true
    }
  assertion r.within_incident_period = false
  assertion r.is_critical_incident_response = false
```

## C2_5_IncidentNotYetClosed

C-2.5: an incident that has been declared but not formally closed has an open
period, so work performed long after declaration is still inside it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_5_IncidentNotYetClosed:
  output r content WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse

scope TestC2_5_IncidentNotYetClosed:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse with {
      -- incident: WTD.CriticalIncident {
           -- severity: 1
           -- declared_at: |2024-05-06|
           -- closed_at: Absent
         }
      -- work_performed_at: |2024-06-30|
      -- performed_in_response_to_incident: true
    }
  assertion r.within_incident_period = true
  assertion r.is_critical_incident_response = true
```

## C2_5_NotYetClosedButBeforeDeclaration

C-2.5: an open period still has a start. Work before declaration is outside it
whether or not the incident has been closed.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_5_NotYetClosedButBeforeDeclaration:
  output r content WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse

scope TestC2_5_NotYetClosedButBeforeDeclaration:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse with {
      -- incident: WTD.CriticalIncident {
           -- severity: 1
           -- declared_at: |2024-05-06|
           -- closed_at: Absent
         }
      -- work_performed_at: |2024-05-05|
      -- performed_in_response_to_incident: true
    }
  assertion r.within_incident_period = false
  assertion r.is_critical_incident_response = false
```

## C2_5_WorkNotInResponseToIncident

C-2.5: 'work performed in response to an incident'. Ordinary work done during
a Severity 1 incident is not Critical Incident Response.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_5_WorkNotInResponseToIncident:
  output r content WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse

scope TestC2_5_WorkNotInResponseToIncident:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.CriticalIncidentResponse with {
      -- incident: WTD.CriticalIncident {
           -- severity: 1
           -- declared_at: |2024-05-06|
           -- closed_at: Present content |2024-05-09|
         }
      -- work_performed_at: |2024-05-07|
      -- performed_in_response_to_incident: false
    }
  assertion r.within_incident_period = true
  assertion r.is_critical_incident_response = false
```

## C2_6_GazettedForThisPlaceOfWork

C-2.6: the day is gazetted for the Employee's principal place of work.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_6_GazettedForThisPlaceOfWork:
  output r content WTD.GazettedPublicHolidays

scope TestC2_6_GazettedForThisPlaceOfWork:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.GazettedPublicHolidays with {
      -- gazette: [
           WTD.GazettedHoliday { -- place_of_work: 1 -- holiday_date: |2024-05-06| };
           WTD.GazettedHoliday { -- place_of_work: 2 -- holiday_date: |2024-07-04| }
         ]
      -- principal_place_of_work: 1
      -- calendar_day: |2024-05-06|
    }
  assertion r.is_gazetted_public_holiday = true
```

## C2_6_GazettedForAnotherPlaceOfWork

C-2.6: 'in the Employee's principal place of work'. A day gazetted elsewhere
is not a Gazetted Public Holiday for this Employee.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_6_GazettedForAnotherPlaceOfWork:
  output r content WTD.GazettedPublicHolidays

scope TestC2_6_GazettedForAnotherPlaceOfWork:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.GazettedPublicHolidays with {
      -- gazette: [
           WTD.GazettedHoliday { -- place_of_work: 1 -- holiday_date: |2024-05-06| };
           WTD.GazettedHoliday { -- place_of_work: 2 -- holiday_date: |2024-07-04| }
         ]
      -- principal_place_of_work: 1
      -- calendar_day: |2024-07-04|
    }
  assertion r.is_gazetted_public_holiday = false
```

## C2_6_DayNotGazettedAnywhere

C-2.6: a day absent from the gazette is an ordinary day.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_6_DayNotGazettedAnywhere:
  output r content WTD.GazettedPublicHolidays

scope TestC2_6_DayNotGazettedAnywhere:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.GazettedPublicHolidays with {
      -- gazette: [
           WTD.GazettedHoliday { -- place_of_work: 1 -- holiday_date: |2024-05-06| }
         ]
      -- principal_place_of_work: 1
      -- calendar_day: |2024-05-07|
    }
  assertion r.is_gazetted_public_holiday = false
```

## C2_6_EmptyGazette

C-2.6: an empty gazette designates nothing.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC2_6_EmptyGazette:
  output r content WTD.GazettedPublicHolidays

scope TestC2_6_EmptyGazette:
  definition r equals
    output of WTD.GazettedPublicHolidays with {
      -- gazette: []
      -- principal_place_of_work: 1
      -- calendar_day: |2024-05-06|
    }
  assertion r.is_gazetted_public_holiday = false
```
